<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>Security Sandbox Vertical – Design</title>
<style>
:root{box-sizing:border-box;padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px);color-scheme:light;--bg:#fff;--card:#fff;--tx:#14213d;--mut:#5b6b85;--ac:#0b6bcb;--ln:#dbe3ee;--ok:#1a8f5a;--wip:#d98a0b;--no:#d6455d}
html{scroll-padding-top:60px}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--tx);font:15px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif}
header{background:#fff;color:var(--tx);padding:28px 20px;border-bottom:4px solid var(--ac)}
header h1{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:1.6rem}header p{margin:0;color:var(--mut);max-width:760px}
nav{position:sticky;top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);z-index:5;background:var(--card);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ln);display:flex;gap:4px;overflow-x:auto;padding:8px 12px}
nav a{white-space:nowrap;color:var(--ac);text-decoration:none;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:8px;font-size:.85rem}
nav a:hover{background:#eef3fa}
main{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:16px}
section{margin:26px 0}
h2{font-size:1.25rem;margin:0 0 4px}.sub{color:var(--mut);margin:0 0 14px;font-size:.9rem}
.grid{display:grid;gap:12px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr))}
.card{background:#fff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(20,33,61,.06);border:1px solid var(--ln);border-radius:12px;padding:14px}
.card h3{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:1rem}.card ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px;color:var(--mut);font-size:.88rem}
.tag{display:inline-block;font-size:.72rem;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:99px;border:1px solid var(--ln);color:var(--mut);margin:2px 2px 0 0}
.flow{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0}
.step{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;position:relative;padding-bottom:14px}
.step:not(:last-child)::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:15px;top:32px;bottom:0;width:2px;background:var(--ln)}
.n{flex:none;width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ac);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:700;font-size:.85rem}
.step .b{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--ln);border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;flex:1}
.step b{display:block}.step span{color:var(--mut);font-size:.87rem}
.two{display:grid;gap:18px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr))}
.lane{font-weight:700;color:var(--ac);margin-bottom:8px}
.dev{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center}
.box{border-radius:10px;padding:12px 14px;text-align:center;font-weight:600;font-size:.88rem;border:2px solid var(--ac);background:var(--card)}
.core{background:#0b6bcb;color:#fff}.tgt{border-color:#d6455d}
.ifs{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px}
.i{font-size:.75rem;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:6px;color:#fff;text-align:center}
.ok{background:var(--ok)}.wip{background:var(--wip)}.no{background:var(--no)}
.arr{font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--mut)}
.tw{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;min-width:560px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--ln);border-radius:10px}
th,td{text-align:left;padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ln);font-size:.87rem;vertical-align:top}
th{background:#f1f5fa;color:var(--mut)}
.st{display:inline-block;padding:2px 9px;border-radius:99px;color:#fff;font-size:.75rem;white-space:nowrap}
.pipe{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap}.pipe .st{background:var(--ac)}
footer{text-align:center;color:var(--mut);font-size:.8rem;padding:20px}
</style></head><body>
<header><h1>Security Sandbox Vertical</h1>
<p>One of the four verticals in the IoT Security Ecosystem &amp; Sandbox WebPortal (C-DAC Bengaluru). Testing and tool execution by C-DAC Hyderabad with IIT Madras, SETS Chennai, Amrita Kollam and IIT Bombay.</p></header>
<nav><a href="#ov">Overview</a><a href="#dom">Domains &amp; Standards</a><a href="#cf">Client Flow</a><a href="#bf">Backend Flow</a><a href="#tools">Tools &amp; Status</a><a href="#dev">Analysis Devices</a><a href="#roles">Roles</a><a href="#open">Open Points</a></nav>
<main>

<section id="ov"><h2>1. Overview</h2><p class="sub">Sandbox = testing tools + testing know-how + process workflow and automation, behind one single sign-on portal.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>Essential security testing tools</h3><ul><li>Built indigenously or customised from open source</li><li>Hardware, firmware, communication, side-channel &amp; crypto</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Testing know-how</h3><ul><li>Procedures with unique IDs and case studies</li><li>Level playing field across all labs</li><li>Standard-agnostic procedures</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Process workflow &amp; automation</h3><ul><li>Choose functional, security, or both</li><li>Questionnaire → job sheet → procedures</li><li>Automated jobs via VMs / exposed API</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Benefit to industry</h3><ul><li>Pre-compliance before costly certification</li><li>Frugal, indigenous tooling</li><li>Pick and choose tests; one-stop point</li></ul></div>
</div></section>

<section id="dom"><h2>2. Application Domains &amp; Standards</h2><p class="sub">The client picks a domain, then a standard; applicable procedures follow from device capabilities.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>Consumer IoT</h3><span class="tag">Smart appliances</span><span class="tag">Gadgets</span><span class="tag">Utilities</span><ul><li>ETSI EN 303 645, NISTIR 8425, OWASP ISVS, STQC essential requirements (future BIS)</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Automotive Electronics</h3><span class="tag">ECU</span><span class="tag">TCU</span><span class="tag">V2V/V2X</span><ul><li>AIS 189/190, ISO/SAE 21434 (TARA)</li><li>CAN, LIN, FlexRay, Auto-Ethernet, UDS, OBD2, XCP</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Industrial Control Systems</h3><span class="tag">PLC</span><span class="tag">SCADA</span><span class="tag">HMI</span><span class="tag">RTU/IED</span><ul><li>IEC 62443 incl. 4-2 (component level)</li><li>Profinet, Modbus, OPC UA, DLMS, EtherCAT</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Medical Devices</h3><span class="tag">Consumer medical</span><span class="tag">Hospital grade</span><ul><li>IEC 60601-4-5</li><li>HL7, DICOM, FHIR</li></ul></div>
</div></section>

<section id="cf"><h2>3. Client-side Flow (WebPortal, Bangalore)</h2><p class="sub">What the manufacturer / user agency does in the portal.</p>
<div class="flow">
<div class="step"><div class="n">1</div><div class="b"><b>Login &amp; select vertical</b><span>Single sign-on → Security Sandbox (functional, security, or both).</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">2</div><div class="b"><b>Register device</b><span>Device class, domain, standard to comply with, device capabilities (interfaces, protocols, OS type).</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">3</div><div class="b"><b>Questionnaire</b><span>Per standard and domain; answers decide the applicable security requirements.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">4</div><div class="b"><b>Job sheet generated</b><span>Questionnaire maps to the list of procedures (by procedure ID) to be run.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">5</div><div class="b"><b>Submit artifacts &amp; device</b><span>Soft artifacts (firmware, docs, PCAPs) uploaded; physical device couriered for hardware tests.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">6</div><div class="b"><b>Submit request</b><span>Request goes to C-DAC Hyderabad (API); status becomes “Submitted”.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">7</div><div class="b"><b>Track status &amp; clarifications</b><span>Live status, clarification requests, additional artifact asks.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">8</div><div class="b"><b>Download report</b><span>Findings, evidence, recommendations; pre-compliance outcome before formal certification.</span></div></div>
</div></section>

<section id="bf"><h2>4. Backend / C-DAC Hyderabad Flow</h2><p class="sub">Lab-side processing after the request arrives.</p>
<div class="flow">
<div class="step"><div class="n">1</div><div class="b"><b>Receive &amp; validate</b><span>Check request, artifacts and device completeness; raise clarification if missing.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">2</div><div class="b"><b>Map to procedures</b><span>Job sheet → repository procedures (description, test requirement, method, case study).</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">3</div><div class="b"><b>Route to tool track</b><span>Hardware · Firmware · Communication · Side-channel &amp; crypto. Automated runs spawn VMs or call partner tools by API; hardware probing is manual.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">4</div><div class="b"><b>Execute &amp; collect evidence</b><span>Logs, dumps, SBOM, PCAP analysis, captures per procedure ID.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">5</div><div class="b"><b>Review &amp; report</b><span>Lab review, consolidated report with severity and recommendations.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">6</div><div class="b"><b>Return to Bangalore</b><span>Status updates and final deliverables pushed to the WebPortal; device returned.</span></div></div>
</div>
<p class="sub" style="margin-top:6px">Proposed status lifecycle:</p>
<div class="pipe"><span class="st">Draft</span><span class="st">Submitted</span><span class="st">Under Validation</span><span class="st">Clarification Needed</span><span class="st">Testing In Progress</span><span class="st">Report Review</span><span class="st">Completed</span><span class="st">Closed</span></div>
</section>

<section id="tools"><h2>5. Tool Tracks &amp; Status (from event slides)</h2><p class="sub">Status as presented in the session; confirm figures before circulating.</p>
<div class="tw"><table>
<tr><th>Track</th><th>Tool / Capability</th><th>Agency</th><th>Status</th></tr>
<tr><td>Hardware</td><td>UHPSA – universal protocol analyser: UART/RS232/422/485, SPI, I²C, JTAG, SWD, CAN, LIN (sniffing, baud detect, pin ID, firmware dump)</td><td>C-DAC HYD</td><td><span class="st ok">Built</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Hardware</td><td>USBIntercept-X – FPGA-based USB sniffer, protocol decode, report generation</td><td>C-DAC HYD</td><td><span class="st ok">Presented</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Firmware</td><td>Static analysis – CVE template matching on firmware; trialled on a Wi-Fi router. Next: API for sandbox integration</td><td>IIT Madras</td><td><span class="st ok">Completed</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Firmware</td><td>Dynamic analysis – runtime behaviour; patent filed. Next: packaging, peer-reviewed publication</td><td>IIT Madras</td><td><span class="st ok">Completed</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Firmware</td><td>Reverse engineering, threat modelling &amp; detection</td><td>IIT Bombay</td><td><span class="st wip">In progress</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Crypto</td><td>Formal verification software tool (ProVerif, CryptoVerif, Frama-C)</td><td>SETS Chennai</td><td><span class="st wip">90%</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Crypto</td><td>Unified formal verification framework (MQTT, TLS1.3, AES, ChaCha20, Poly1305…)</td><td>SETS Chennai</td><td><span class="st wip">50%</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Privacy</td><td>Privacy analysis framework (PIA, anonymisation validation)</td><td>SETS Chennai</td><td><span class="st no">20%</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Comm.</td><td>MUD profile verification, provisioning lifecycle, cellular IoT validation</td><td>Amrita Kollam</td><td><span class="st wip">In progress</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Comm.</td><td>IPv6 testing; AI/ML anomaly detection on PCAPs</td><td>SETS / C-DAC</td><td><span class="st wip">Planned</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Side-channel</td><td>EM, timing, power analysis algorithms (existing scopes/probes)</td><td>IIT Madras</td><td><span class="st wip">In progress</span></td></tr>
</table></div></section>

<section id="dev"><h2>6. Analysis Devices (cleaned from slides)</h2><p class="sub">Interface readiness: green completed · amber partial · red not started.</p>
<div class="two">
<div class="card"><div class="lane">Embedded Protocols Security Analysis Device</div>
<div class="dev"><div class="box">Host PC</div><span class="arr">⇄</span><div class="box core">H/W Security<br>Analysis Device</div>
<div class="ifs"><span class="i ok">UART</span><span class="i ok">SPI</span><span class="i ok">I2C</span><span class="i ok">RS232</span><span class="i ok">RS485</span><span class="i wip">JTAG</span><span class="i wip">SWD</span><span class="i no">CAN</span><span class="i no">USB</span></div>
<span class="arr">⇄</span><div class="box tgt">Target Device</div></div>
<p class="sub" style="margin-top:10px">Low-end embedded (Cortex-M, bare metal). Outcomes: pin identification, passive attack, active attack.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="lane">Communication Security Analysis Device</div>
<div class="dev"><div class="box">Host PC</div><span class="arr">⇄</span><div class="box core">Comm. Security<br>Analysis Device</div>
<div class="ifs"><span class="i ok">Ethernet</span><span class="i ok">Wi-Fi</span><span class="i wip">Bluetooth</span><span class="i no">Zigbee</span><span class="i no">LoRa</span></div>
<span class="arr">⇄</span><div class="box tgt">Target Device</div></div>
<p class="sub" style="margin-top:10px">High-end embedded (Cortex-A, embedded Linux). Outcomes: passive attack, active attack.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section id="roles"><h2>7. Stakeholders on the Portal</h2>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>Product manufacturer / User agency</h3><ul><li>Submit devices, view reports</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Testing lab</h3><ul><li>Empanelled labs run job sheets using sandbox procedures</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>R&amp;D / Academic</h3><ul><li>Contribute procedures, tools, methodologies</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Certification body</h3><ul><li>BIS, STQC, CERT-In, NCIIPC can log in to view results</li></ul></div>
</div>
<p class="sub" style="margin-top:12px">Tool deployment: loosely coupled (partner tools via exposed API) or physical set-up inside the sandbox in Bangalore. Related scheme: Bharat Cyber Trust Mark (4 grades, 2 scores, QR-linked repository).</p></section>

<section id="open"><h2>8. Open Points for Hyderabad Discussion</h2>
<div class="card"><ul>
<li>API contract for request submission, status updates and report return</li>
<li>Mandatory device details, firmware and documents per domain</li>
<li>Which tests are automated vs manual; physical device logistics</li>
<li>Status transitions and report format / deliverables</li>
<li>Roadmap per tool for portal integration (static, dynamic, formal verification APIs)</li>
</ul></div></section>
</main>
<footer>Draft design · based on IoT Sandbox 2026 session</footer>
</body></html>
